#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e28d33c6-9b54-5018-8c30-20b4328565a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331941} {:answer/id #uuid "f64f7624-f5e2-5746-81d4-517943568d06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331942} {:answer/id #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331943} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab1012d-433c-5c61-b762-c95a6cfddbbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331944} {:answer/id #uuid "aab72c3b-3e42-516f-81fc-8d253ba110c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd34680-796d-5b2d-a195-fe32a22dd5ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "384d449f-273e-593f-9d4d-a9fdf55ff2d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126359" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$ about $x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331955} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a61a26-d697-50e5-9a14-f09ca5b0e334" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "783fb36c-345a-5c94-9d91-f565c09ac763" :question/math-academy-id "q-351859" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{-2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1-2x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4{e}^{-0}=4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8{e}^{-0}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-2\\cdot x+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-2x+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
